{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(data: list[tuple]) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    If the input list is empty, it returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return None\n\n    min_second_value = float('inf')\n    result_first_value = None\n\n    for item_tuple in data:\n        current_first_value = item_tuple[0]\n        current_second_value = item_tuple[1]\n\n        # Update if a strictly smaller second value is found, handling ties by keeping the earlier item.\n        if current_second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = current_second_value\n            result_first_value = current_first_value\n\n    return result_first_value"}
