{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning its digits strictly alternate between two distinct values.\n    Example: 1212121 (True), 123 (False), 112 (False), 7 (False).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert number to a list of its digits\n    s = str(abs(number))\n    digits = [int(d) for d in s]\n\n    # Numbers with less than 2 digits cannot be undulating\n    if len(digits) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    digit_a = digits[0]\n    digit_b = digits[1]\n\n    # The first two distinct digits must be different for undulating pattern\n    if digit_a == digit_b:\n        return False\n\n    # Check the rest of the digits for the alternating pattern\n    for i in range(2, len(digits)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index should match digit_a\n            if digits[i] != digit_a:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd index should match digit_b\n            if digits[i] != digit_b:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
