{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than the input integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _get_number_as_string(num: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Converts an integer to its string representation.\"\"\"\n        return str(num)\n\n    def _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Reverses a given string.\"\"\"\n        return s[::-1]\n\n    def _get_left_half(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Extracts the left half of a number's string representation.\"\"\"\n        length = len(s)\n        return s[:(length + 1) // 2]\n\n    def _construct_palindrome_str(left_half: str, is_odd_length: bool) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Constructs a palindrome string from its left half and length parity.\"\"\"\n        if is_odd_length:\n            return left_half + _reverse_string(left_half[:-1])\n        else:\n            return left_half + _reverse_string(left_half)\n\n    def _increment_left_half(left_half: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Increments the string representation of the left half of a number.\"\"\"\n        num = int(left_half)\n        num += 1\n        return str(num)\n\n    s_n = _get_number_as_string(n)\n    length = len(s_n)\n    current_is_odd_length = (length % 2 != 0)\n\n    current_left_half = _get_left_half(s_n)\n\n    # Calculate an initial candidate palindrome based on n's structure.\n    candidate_palindrome_str = _construct_palindrome_str(current_left_half, current_is_odd_length)\n    candidate_palindrome = int(candidate_palindrome_str)\n\n    # If this candidate is already strictly greater than n, it's the answer.\n    if candidate_palindrome > n:\n        return candidate_palindrome\n    \n    # If not, we need to increment the left half to find the next palindrome.\n    old_left_half_len = len(current_left_half)\n    current_left_half = _increment_left_half(current_left_half)\n    new_left_half_len = len(current_left_half)\n\n    # If incrementing the left half added a digit (e.g., \"9\" to \"10\", \"99\" to \"100\"),\n    # the resulting palindrome will always have an odd number of digits (e.g., 101, 10001).\n    if new_left_half_len > old_left_half_len:\n        current_is_odd_length = True\n\n    # Construct the final palindrome using the (potentially updated) left half and parity.\n    final_palindrome_str = _construct_palindrome_str(current_left_half, current_is_odd_length)\n    return int(final_palindrome_str)"}
