{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list[Any]]) -> set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Finds elements common to all sub-lists within a given nested list.\n    Returns a set of these common elements.\"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_elements with the set of the first sub-list\n    # If the first sub-list is empty, common_elements will be an empty set\n    common_elements = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining sub-lists and find their intersection\n    for sublist in nested_list[1:]:\n        current_set = set(sublist)\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(current_set)\n        # If common_elements becomes empty at any point,\n        # no more common elements can be found, so we can return early.\n        if not common_elements:\n            return set()\n\n    return common_elements"}
