{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of odd-valued decimal equivalents generated by rotating\n    a binary string a specified number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n    n = len(binary_string)\n\n    for _ in range(rotations_count):\n        # A binary number is odd if its last digit is '1'.\n        # This check is more efficient than converting to int and then checking modulo.\n        if current_binary_string[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        # Rotate the string by moving the first character to the end\n        current_binary_string = current_binary_string[1:] + current_binary_string[0]\n        \n    return odd_count"}
