{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(list_of_items: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    Returns None if the list is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not list_of_items:\n        return None\n\n    frequency_map = {}\n    for item in list_of_items:\n        frequency_map[item] = frequency_map.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    # Find the item (key) with the maximum count (value)\n    max_item = max(frequency_map, key=frequency_map.get)\n\n    return max_item"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix_data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given matrix is a magic square.\n    This function initializes a Matrix object and uses a MagicSquareChecker to perform the validation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Matrix:\n        \"\"\"\n        Represents a two-dimensional array and provides methods for matrix-specific properties and calculations.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, elements):\n            self._elements = elements\n            self._num_rows = len(elements)\n            self._num_cols = len(elements[0]) if elements else 0\n            # If the matrix is not empty, ensure all rows have the same number of columns.\n            # The problem context implies valid matrix structures for simplicity.\n\n        def is_square(self):\n            \"\"\"Determines if the matrix has an equal number of rows and columns and is not empty.\"\"\"\n            return self._num_rows > 0 and self._num_rows == self._num_cols\n\n        def get_size(self):\n            \"\"\"Returns the dimension of the square matrix (number of rows).\"\"\"\n            return self._num_rows\n\n        def get_sum_of_row(self, row_index):\n            \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in the specified row.\"\"\"\n            return sum(self._elements[row_index])\n\n        def get_sum_of_column(self, col_index):\n            \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in the specified column.\"\"\"\n            return sum(self._elements[i][col_index] for i in range(self._num_rows))\n\n        def get_sum_of_main_diagonal(self):\n            \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the main diagonal.\"\"\"\n            return sum(self._elements[i][i] for i in range(self._num_rows))\n\n        def get_sum_of_anti_diagonal(self):\n            \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the anti-diagonal.\"\"\"\n            size = self._num_rows\n            return sum(self._elements[i][size - 1 - i] for i in range(size))\n\n    class MagicSquareChecker:\n        \"\"\"\n        Orchestrates the process of checking if a given matrix is a magic square.\n        \"\"\"\n        def check(self, matrix):\n            \"\"\"Determines if the provided Matrix object is a magic square.\"\"\"\n            if not matrix.is_square():\n                return False\n\n            size = matrix.get_size()\n            if size == 0:\n                return False # An empty matrix is not a magic square\n\n            # Calculate the expected magic sum from the first row\n            magic_sum = matrix.get_sum_of_row(0)\n\n            # Check row sums\n            for i in range(size):\n                if matrix.get_sum_of_row(i) != magic_sum:\n                    return False\n\n            # Check column sums\n            for i in range(size):\n                if matrix.get_sum_of_column(i) != magic_sum:\n                    return False\n\n            # Check main diagonal sum\n            if matrix.get_sum_of_main_diagonal() != magic_sum:\n                return False\n\n            # Check anti-diagonal sum\n            if matrix.get_sum_of_anti_diagonal() != magic_sum:\n                return False\n\n            return True\n\n    matrix_obj = Matrix(matrix_data)\n    checker = MagicSquareChecker()\n    return checker.check(matrix_obj)"}
