{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(numbers: list[int], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range.\n    Raises ValueError if indices are invalid (out of bounds, negative, or start > end).\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    # Validate indices are non-negative and within list bounds.\n    if not (0 <= start_index < list_length and 0 <= end_index < list_length):\n        if list_length == 0 and (start_index != 0 or end_index != -1):\n            raise ValueError(\"Indices out of bounds for an empty list.\")\n        elif list_length > 0 and (start_index < 0 or end_index < 0 or start_index >= list_length or end_index >= list_length):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Indices must be non-negative and within list bounds [0, {list_length-1}]. Got start={start_index}, end={end_index}.\")\n\n    # Validate start index is not greater than end index.\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Start index ({start_index}) must be less than or equal to end index ({end_index}).\")\n\n    # Calculate the sum of numbers in the specified range (inclusive).\n    current_sum = 0\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        current_sum += numbers[i]\n\n    return current_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(input_number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (binary digits with value 1) in a given integer.\n    The `bin()` function returns a string representation, including '0b' prefix and a '-' for negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    return bin(input_number).count('1')"}
