{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list, n: int, x: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if x is a majority element in sorted array arr of length n, occurring strictly more than n/2 times. Returns True if it is, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    \n    majority_threshold = n / 2\n\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of x using binary search (lower bound).\n    first_idx = -1\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            first_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Look for an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    if first_idx == -1: # If x is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n        return False\n\n    # Count occurrences starting from first_idx.\n    count = 0\n    current_idx = first_idx\n    while current_idx < n and arr[current_idx] == x:\n        count += 1\n        current_idx += 1\n\n    return count > majority_threshold"}
