{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string using dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] will store the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                # If characters match, they contribute 2 to the LPS, plus the LPS of the inner substring\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of excluding the first or last character\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The result for the entire string is stored in dp[0][n-1]\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
