{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous sub-array in the modified array formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    Utilizes Kadane's algorithm and considers cases based on the total sum of the array.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _kadane(current_arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Implements Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum contiguous sub-array sum.\n        Handles cases where all numbers are negative, returning the largest negative number or 0 if empty.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not current_arr:\n            return 0\n        \n        current_max = current_arr[0]\n        global_max = current_arr[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(current_arr)):\n            current_max = max(current_arr[i], current_max + current_arr[i])\n            global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n        \n        return global_max\n\n    if k == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Case 1: k = 1\n    if k == 1:\n        return _kadane(arr)\n\n    # Case 2: k > 1\n    max_sum_single_arr = _kadane(arr)\n    total_sum_arr = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate max prefix sum\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    max_prefix_sum_arr = -float('inf')\n    for x in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum_arr = max(max_prefix_sum_arr, current_prefix_sum)\n    \n    # Calculate max suffix sum\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    max_suffix_sum_arr = -float('inf')\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix_sum_arr = max(max_suffix_sum_arr, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is negative, repeating it multiple times won't improve the max sum beyond 2 repetitions.\n    # The maximum sum must either be within a single 'arr' or span at most two 'arr's.\n    if total_sum_arr < 0:\n        return max(max_sum_single_arr, _kadane(arr + arr))\n    else:\n        # If total sum is non-negative, the maximum sum can span across repetitions.\n        # It's the max suffix sum + (k-2) * total_sum + max prefix sum.\n        # Compare this with the max sum found within a single array.\n        max_sum_spanning = max_prefix_sum_arr + max_suffix_sum_arr + (k - 2) * total_sum_arr\n        return max(max_sum_single_arr, max_sum_spanning)"}
