{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for a given non-negative integer n.\n    The sum is determined by the equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n), where division implies integer division.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for each number in a given list.\n    e.g., [10, 2, 56] -> 14\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_single_of_digits(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of digits for a single integer, using its absolute value.\n        e.g., 10 -> 1, 56 -> 11, -123 -> 6\n        \"\"\"\n        abs_number = abs(number)\n        digit_sum = 0\n        for digit_char in str(abs_number):\n            digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n        return digit_sum\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_sum += _calculate_single_of_digits(num)\n    return total_sum"}
