{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(numbers: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    Returns the two integers as a tuple, raising ValueError if the input has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least two elements\")\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    # The highest product can come from two largest numbers or two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    # Compare the product of the two smallest with the product of the two largest.\n    \n    product_of_smallest_two = sorted_numbers[0] * sorted_numbers[1]\n    pair_smallest = (sorted_numbers[0], sorted_numbers[1])\n\n    product_of_largest_two = sorted_numbers[-1] * sorted_numbers[-2]\n    pair_largest = (sorted_numbers[-2], sorted_numbers[-1])\n\n    if product_of_smallest_two > product_of_largest_two:\n        return pair_smallest\n    else:\n        return pair_largest"}
