{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of tuple elements, including nested tuples.\n    It iterates through corresponding elements, multiplying numbers or recursively processing inner tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for elem1, elem2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if isinstance(elem1, tuple) and isinstance(elem2, tuple):\n            result.append(index_multiplication(elem1, elem2))\n        else:\n            result.append(elem1 * elem2)\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "def find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first adverb and its positions in a sentence.\n    Returns a tuple (start_index, end_index, adverb_string) if an adverb is found, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    import re\n    import string\n    from typing import Optional, Tuple\n\n    def _clean_word(word: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Removes leading/trailing punctuation from a word.\"\"\"\n        return word.strip(string.punctuation)\n\n    def _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a word is an adverb based on simple rules (e.g., ends in 'ly').\"\"\"\n        return word.lower().endswith('ly')\n\n    words_with_indices = []\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\S+', sentence):\n        word_text = match.group(0)\n        start_idx = match.start(0)\n        end_idx = match.end(0)\n        words_with_indices.append((word_text, start_idx, end_idx))\n\n    for original_word, start_idx, end_idx_original in words_with_indices:\n        cleaned_word = _clean_word(original_word)\n        if cleaned_word and _is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            leading_punctuation_len = len(original_word) - len(original_word.lstrip(string.punctuation))\n            actual_start_index = start_idx + leading_punctuation_len\n            actual_end_index = actual_start_index + len(cleaned_word)\n            return (actual_start_index, actual_end_index, cleaned_word)\n\n    return None"}
