{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    elif n == 0:\n        return 3  # P(0) = 3\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 3  # P(0) + P(1) = 3 + 0 = 3\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 5  # P(0) + P(1) + P(2) = 3 + 0 + 2 = 5\n\n    # Initialize the first three Perrin numbers: P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    p0, p1, p2 = 3, 0, 2\n    # Initialize sum with the first three numbers\n    current_sum = p0 + p1 + p2\n\n    # Calculate subsequent Perrin numbers and add to sum\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        pk = p0 + p1  # P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3)\n        current_sum += pk\n        # Shift numbers for the next iteration: p0 becomes P(k-2), p1 becomes P(k-1), p2 becomes P(k)\n        p0, p1, p2 = p1, p2, pk\n\n    return current_sum"}
