{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\ndef combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Generates all possible combinations of elements from the input_list.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list of elements (e.g., strings, numbers).\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of lists, where each inner list is a combination of elements\n        from the input_list, including the empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_combinations = [[]]  # Initialize with the empty list (FR2)\n\n    for element in input_list:  # For each element in input_list (FR3)\n        newly_created_combinations = []\n        for existing_combination in all_combinations:\n            # Create new_combination by prepending the current element (FR4)\n            new_combination = [element] + existing_combination\n            newly_created_combinations.append(new_combination)\n        # Append newly created combinations to the overall list (FR5)\n        all_combinations.extend(newly_created_combinations)\n\n    return all_combinations\n```"}
