{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns numbers that occur exactly once in an input list,\n    preserving their relative order of first appearance.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    unique_ordered_list = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            unique_ordered_list.append(num)\n\n    return unique_ordered_list"}
