{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1: list[int], array2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth smallest element from two given sorted arrays using a merge-like approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    p1, p2 = 0, 0\n    current_k = 0\n    result = -1\n\n    while p1 < len(array1) and p2 < len(array2):\n        current_k += 1\n        if array1[p1] < array2[p2]:\n            result = array1[p1]\n            p1 += 1\n        else:\n            result = array2[p2]\n            p2 += 1\n        if current_k == k:\n            return result\n\n    while p1 < len(array1):\n        current_k += 1\n        result = array1[p1]\n        p1 += 1\n        if current_k == k:\n            return result\n\n    while p2 < len(array2):\n        current_k += 1\n        result = array2[p2]\n        p2 += 1\n        if current_k == k:\n            return result"}
