{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of equal size.\n    Assumes lists are sorted and of equal size 'n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    idx_list1, idx_list2 = 0, 0\n    median1, median2 = 0, 0 \n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the elements at positions (n-1) and n\n    # in the combined sorted list of 2n elements.\n    for _ in range(n + 1):\n        if idx_list1 == n:\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list2[idx_list2]\n            idx_list2 += 1\n        elif idx_list2 == n:\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list1[idx_list1]\n            idx_list1 += 1\n        elif list1[idx_list1] < list2[idx_list2]:\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list1[idx_list1]\n            idx_list1 += 1\n        else:\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list2[idx_list2]\n            idx_list2 += 1\n\n    return (median1 + median2) / 2.0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def _is_divisible_pair(a: int, b: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a is divisible by b or b is divisible by a, handling zero.\"\"\"\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return True\n    if a == 0: # If a is 0, then 0 % b == 0 for any b != 0.\n        return True\n    if b == 0: # If b is 0, then 0 % a == 0 for any a != 0.\n        return True\n    return a % b == 0 or b % a == 0\n\ndef largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is mutually divisible.\n    This uses dynamic programming on a sorted version of the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n    dp = [1] * n  # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with sorted_numbers[i]\n\n    max_size = 1\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if _is_divisible_pair(sorted_numbers[i], sorted_numbers[j]):\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n\n    return max_size"}
