{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(center_coordinate: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts all adjacent coordinates of the given coordinate tuple.\n\n    Returns a list of 3x3 grid coordinates centered at the input, sorted by x then y.\n    \"\"\"\n    center_x, center_y = center_coordinate\n    adjacent_coordinates = []\n\n    # Generate coordinates for the 3x3 grid, including the center\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):  # dx values: -1, 0, 1\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):  # dy values: -1, 0, 1\n            new_x = center_x + dx\n            new_y = center_y + dy\n            adjacent_coordinates.append([new_x, new_y])\n\n    # Sort the coordinates first by x-value, then by y-value\n    adjacent_coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], coord[1]))\n\n    return adjacent_coordinates"}
