{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    def _heapify(arr_inner: list, n_inner: int, i_inner: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to maintain the max-heap property in a subtree rooted at index i.\n        \"\"\"\n        largest = i_inner\n        left_child = 2 * i_inner + 1\n        right_child = 2 * i_inner + 2\n\n        if left_child < n_inner and arr_inner[left_child] > arr_inner[largest]:\n            largest = left_child\n\n        if right_child < n_inner and arr_inner[right_child] > arr_inner[largest]:\n            largest = right_child\n\n        if largest != i_inner:\n            arr_inner[i_inner], arr_inner[largest] = arr_inner[largest], arr_inner[i_inner]\n            _heapify(arr_inner, n_inner, largest)\n\n    def _build_max_heap(arr_inner: list, n_inner: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to build a max-heap from an array.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Start from the last non-leaf node and heapify upwards\n        for i_inner in range(n_inner // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n            _heapify(arr_inner, n_inner, i_inner)\n\n    _build_max_heap(arr, n)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Move current root to end\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call max heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
