{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "def power_base_sum(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all digits of the base to the specified power.\n    This function orchestrates the power calculation, digit extraction, and summation using helper functions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_power(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes base raised to power, utilizing Python's arbitrary-precision integers.\"\"\"\n        return base ** power\n\n    def _extract_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Converts a large integer into a list of its individual digits.\"\"\"\n        return [int(digit) for digit in str(number)]\n\n    def _sum_digits(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of a list of individual integer digits.\"\"\"\n        return sum(digits)\n\n    # _validate_inputs is omitted as per prompt constraints (no isinstance() checks or exception raising).\n    \n    power_result = _calculate_power(base, power)\n    digits_list = _extract_digits(power_result)\n    final_sum = _sum_digits(digits_list)\n    return final_sum"}
