{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with `n` digits.\n    Iteratively calculates triangular numbers and their digit counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    def _calculate_triangular_number(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the k-th triangular number.\"\"\"\n        return k * (k + 1) // 2\n\n    import math\n\n    def _get_digit_count(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Determines the number of digits in a positive integer.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return 1\n        return math.floor(math.log10(number)) + 1\n\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = _calculate_triangular_number(k)\n        digit_count = _get_digit_count(triangular_number)\n\n        if digit_count == n:\n            return k\n        elif digit_count > n:\n            # If the digit count exceeds n, it means we've overshot.\n            # For a given n, there should always be a triangular number\n            # with exactly n digits. This case should ideally not be reached\n            # before finding a match for valid n.\n            pass # Continue to increment k in case of unexpected scenario\n        k += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/742", "solution": "import math\n\ndef area_tetrahedron(side_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the surface area of a regular tetrahedron by delegating to an internal Tetrahedron class.\"\"\"\n\n    class Tetrahedron:\n        \"\"\"Represents a regular tetrahedron and calculates its surface area.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, side_length: float):\n            self._side_length = float(side_length)\n\n        def calculate_area(self) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Calculates the total surface area of the regular tetrahedron using the formula sqrt(3) * a^2.\"\"\"\n            return math.sqrt(3) * (self._side_length ** 2)\n\n    tetrahedron = Tetrahedron(side_length)\n    return tetrahedron.calculate_area()"}
