{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every digit it contains.\n    Numbers containing the digit '0' are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _get_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts the constituent digits of an integer.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_num = number\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return digits[::-1] # Reverse to get digits in order\n\n    def _contains_zero(digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a list of digits contains the digit '0'.\"\"\"\n        return 0 in digits\n\n    def _is_divisible_by_all_digits(number: int, digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verifies if a number is perfectly divisible by each of its constituent digits.\"\"\"\n        for digit in digits:\n            if number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    result_list = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if num == 0: # Special case for 0, if it were allowed in the range\n            continue\n        \n        digits = _get_digits(num)\n\n        if not _contains_zero(digits):\n            if _is_divisible_by_all_digits(num, digits):\n                result_list.append(num)\n    \n    return result_list"}
